+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Patch applyPatch (RFC 6902)"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Request
+
+Implement JSON Patch (RFC 6902): export `applyPatch(document, patch)` from `src/index.ts`. It applies an
+array of operations (add, remove, replace, move, copy, test) and returns the result as a new value, without
+mutating its input. It throws when the patch is invalid or an operation fails.
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- The input document and the patch are never mutated; values inserted are copies.
+- add: parent must exist; arrays accept index 0..length and "-"; "" replaces the document.
+- remove/replace: target must exist; removing the whole document throws.
+- move/copy: "from" must exist; moving a value into its own child throws.
+- test: deep equality (object key order ignored); a mismatch throws.
+- Invalid patches throw: non-array, non-object operation, unknown op, missing path/value/from.
+- Members like `__proto__` are plain members; no prototype pollution.
